<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n61708" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Λᾰκεδαίμ-ων</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ονος</span>, ἡ, voc. -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>
		v.l. in
		<i><span class="en">
			Pi.
			<u>P.</u>
			10.1
		</span></i>:—<u>Lacedaemon</u>, the capital of Laconia,
			<i><span class="en">
			Od.
			13.414
		</span></i>, etc.; also, <u>Laconia</u> itself, <i><span class="en">
			Il.
			2.581
		</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
			Hdt.
			1.67
		</span></i>, etc.: also as Adj., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Διὸς Λακεδαίμονος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					6.56
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Λ. γῆς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Hel.</u>
					474
				</span></i>
			:—but regul. Adj.
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Λακεδαιμόνιος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, of
			persons, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				7.228
			</span></i>, etc., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Λακωνικός</span> being
			commonly used of things; but 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Λακεδαιμόνιοι ἀστέρες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Call.
					<u>Lav.Pall.</u>
					24
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
